WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:06.110
The long wait for Avengers: Endgame is almost
over, and if its test audiences are any indication,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.260
it'll be well worth it.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.140
In a recent conversation with BoxOfficePro.com,
co-director Joe Russo revealed that the final

00:00:12.159 --> 00:00:16.980
film in the Infinity Saga has scored perhaps
the best reception of any MCU film to date,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.140
which, of course, is no small feat.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.000
Like all tentpole films, each new MCU entry
is put through a gauntlet of test audiences

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.760
before it hits your local multiplex.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.600
Russo explained that these screenings are
often used to fine-tune certain scenes, tweak

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.240
certain elements of the plot, or streamline
the narrative.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.280
"We try to create a density in storytelling
that makes [each film] feel compulsive.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.700
We're very rigorous about storytelling points,
and we spend months in the edit room twisting

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.220
and turning the narrative a bunch of different
ways until we think we've unlocked the best

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:44.720
one.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.340
We're vigilant about using test audiences
to tell us whether we're on the right track

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.220
or we're making bad decisions.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.330
With Endgame, it had one of the most incredible
audience responses in Marvel history.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.360
Irrespective of the length, it's been consistently
embraced by the test audiences."

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:02.380
To put that in perspective, consider that
MCU flicks tend to fare very well with these

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.600
audiences in general, and more than one recent
entry has completely blown crowds away at

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.620
early screenings.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.440
Captain Marvel, for example, was heralded
as one of the best films in the entirety of

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.860
the MCU, while 2017's Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 2 received a perfect score of 100 from

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.820
its test audiences, which is virtually unheard
of.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.980
It goes without saying that expectations are
sky high for Endgame, which will put a cap

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:28.810
on an overarching narrative spanning eleven
years, 22 films, and dozens of individual

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.810
character arcs.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:33.370
Yet, at least as far as test audiences are
concerned, it seems to have more than met

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.560
those expectations.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:39.520
So how did brothers Joe and Anthony Russo
manage such a massively complex undertaking?

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.320
It turns out their entire careers have prepared
them for this moment.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.200
Not only have they already helmed three of
the MCU's most challenging ensembles with

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.440
Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Captain
America: Civil War, and Avengers: Infinity

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.800
War, but prior to joining Marvel, they earned
a reputation for deftly weaving complicated

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.520
storylines on the cult classic sitcoms Arrested
Development and Community.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.180
Joe Russo told BoxOfficePro,

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.600
"We spent a decade squeezing complex comedy
stories with many, many characters, both of

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.660
those shows being big ensemble shows, into
21 minutes.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.420
We'd call it 'the Russo path,' where we came
in and squeezed it down to a density that

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.829
we felt would elevate the show, because it
would move so quickly that you'd miss half

00:02:14.829 --> 00:02:16.700
the jokes and have to watch it again.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.000
That was an agenda of ours.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.480
The same thing is true when we work on these
Marvel films."

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.659
It's a method that has worked out pretty well
for the filmmaking pair.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.820
But while it's been speculated that Endgame
could constitute their MCU swan song, Russo

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.900
isn't ready to make that call just yet.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.540
"The door is always open.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.420
Everyone at Marvel is like family to us.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.160
We grew up reading comic books, and these
stories are incredibly open to us.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.180
Anything that moved you as a child or spoke
to you as a child has an emotional resonance

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.840
you carry with you your entire life.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.080
It's very hard to find a story that can speak
to you the same way it did when you were younger."

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.760
"I keep telling everybody they should move
on.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.100
Some do.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:54.420
But not us."

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.410
It goes without saying that fans across the
board would love to see the Russos continue

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.689
on in the MCU, but if they end up departing
after Endgame, it looks like they'll be going

00:03:02.689 --> 00:03:03.500
out with a bang.

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:08.180
And in case the rapturous reception from test
audiences isn't enough to convince you, consider

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.120
the reaction of Captain America himself.

00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:14.180
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
the star was nearly at a loss for words when

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.540
asked to describe his Endgame viewing experience,
finally saying,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.180
"Man, this one's really good.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.960
I choked up like three times."

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.960
All of which is to say: buckle up, true believers.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.900
Avengers: Endgame is nothing less than the
culmination of the single most ambitious feat

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.469
of storytelling in cinematic history, and
all signs point to Mighty Marvel having completely

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:33.120
nailed it.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.800
We'll get to see for ourselves just how hard
when the flick hits screens on April 26.

